      "why": "The RETNET paper in this depot is the published study protocol and reports no outcome data of any kind — no response, no progression-free survival, no survival. Its quantitative content is a power calculation resting on retrospective single-centre estimates of 11 months of hepatic progression-free survival for bland embolisation against 20 for lipiodol chemoembolisation, with the assumption that lipiodol and drug-eluting chemoembolisation are equivalent on safety, which the trial itself then disproved. Its practice-changing message came from the 20% serious-adverse-event stopping rule that closed the drug-eluting-bead arm, a closure reported in the ENETS 2024 guidance rather than in the protocol paper. Any outcome figure attributed to RETNET anywhere in the programme's material — including the shared liver-directed-therapy matrix, which carries such figures for this disease — is unsourced and should be removed at source.",
